---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import Draft from '../../components/Draft.astro';
import { address, company, email } from '../../lib/entity';
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Privacy', description: 'What version.cam keeps about you, where, and for how long.' }}>
	<Draft />
	<p>
		{company}, {address}, is the controller of the personal data described here. This page covers the hosted
		service; the versioncam package runs on your machines and in your CI, and sends us nothing unless you run{' '}
		<code>versioncam publish</code>.
	</p>

	<h2>What we keep, and why</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Your GitHub identity</strong>: your GitHub id, login and, if GitHub shares it, your email address,
			and which accounts you belong to. To sign you in and to show you your projects.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>What your CI publishes</strong>: recordings (the timeline and the screens of your app), the files
			rendered from them, and the commit, branch and run they came from. To provide the service. If your screens
			show personal data, you are its controller and we process it for you only.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Billing</strong>: your plan, your billing email and address, and your VAT number if you give one.
			Stripe takes your card; we never see it.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>What keeps the service running</strong>: counts of publishes and renders, and the IP addresses of
			requests to our forms, kept for an hour to stop abuse. The services form is checked by Cloudflare
			Turnstile, which looks at your browser, never at what you type, to tell a person from a bot; we learn only
			whether the check passed.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Where</h2>
	<p>
		Recordings, renders and our database are stored in the European Union, in Cloudflare's EU jurisdiction.
		Rendering runs on Cloudflare's network, which may process a recording outside the EU for the seconds a
		render takes. Our providers are listed on the <a href="/legal/subprocessors/">subprocessors</a> page.
	</p>

	<h2>How long</h2>
	<p>
		Recordings are kept as your plan and your project's settings say, and removed within an hour of your
		deleting them, with copies in backups gone within 30 days. Account data is kept while you have an account;
		invoices are kept for as long as tax law requires.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies</h2>
	<p>
		One cookie, which keeps you signed in, and one that lasts the ten minutes of signing in with GitHub. No
		tracking and no analytics cookies. The services page runs Cloudflare Turnstile, under Cloudflare's{' '}
		<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Turnstile privacy addendum</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>
		You may ask for a copy of your data, its correction, its deletion, or its transfer, and object to how we use
		it: write to {email}. You may also complain to the Information Commissioner of the Republic of Slovenia, or
		to the authority where you live.
	</p>
</StarlightPage>
